.render/

# Match footage. The full broadcast is not ours to redistribute and never
# goes in here.
#
# The seven clips the session itself walks through are the exception, and the
# reasoning is worth writing down rather than leaving as an inconsistency. A
# deployed build with no footage shows a coach a black rectangle with chalk
# floating on it, which misrepresents the product more than a short excerpt
# does. These are seconds-long cuts around a single pass, kept for
# demonstration; the match they came from is not here and cannot be
# reassembled from them.
#
# The twelve per-player clips stay out. They are not on the path a visitor
# walks, the interface says plainly that they run locally, and thirty
# megabytes is not worth spending to avoid a sentence.
/public/tape/
/public/clips/*
# Stills cut from the broadcast for calibration. Frames of the footage are the
# footage, and the whole project keeps it out of the repository. Only the
# homography derived from them is committed.
/public/calib/

# ── Backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
results/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
hydradb-data/
*.pt
*.mkv
*.mp4
sn-data/
.playwright-mcp/
*.png
# Generated by scripts/use-workspace.mjs from the selected workspace.
src/content/snapshots/active/

# The seven the session walks through, un-ignored last.
#
# Git takes the last matching rule, and `*.mp4` above this catches everything
# regardless of what an earlier negation said. That is why these sat next to
# their own exceptions for a whole deploy and still 404ed in production: the
# rule was written, it was just outvoted.
!/public/clips/008_25.mp4
!/public/clips/031_25.mp4
!/public/clips/063_07.mp4
!/public/clips/072_21.mp4
!/public/clips/goal_079_24.mp4
!/public/clips/goal_080_59.mp4
!/public/clips/goal_117_05.mp4

# Working notes, not the product.
#
# The submission draft and the video shot list are ours to write in and are
# still being written in; a judge finding a form answer with "to fill in" next
# to it learns something true and unhelpful. They stay on disk and out of the
# repository.
/docs/SUBMISSION.md
/docs/VIDEO.md
/docs/superpowers/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
